\paragraph{Historical seed consistency.}
The exploratory cohort's original 5-seed evaluation (Table~\ref{tab:fol-beta01-perseed}) showed 2/5 ISR seeds H7-dominated (s43: $97\%$, s44: $100\%$) and 3/5 with H1-dominant hacking but low H7.
This is directionally consistent with the matched cohort's 5/5 H7 domination: the exploratory cohort's lower H7 rate likely reflects seed-dependent stochasticity rather than a qualitative difference, as extended training of the non-H7 seeds (s42, s45) confirmed eventual convergence to H7 or reward collapse.
Exploratory seeds are not included in the matched-design statistical tests to preserve the independence assumption.

